{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision: land the tooling head now, locally, under approval\n`882aba2f`. It delivers GS-3 and FH-1.\n\n1. Ratify `882aba2f` and merge head `720f228a` into the shared\n   checkout. Main is `4b198d0f`, and it is an ancestor of the head.\n2. The merge must bind both reports. Read back both closures, GS-3\n   (a187a745) and FH-1 (1be80098), and state them in the landing\n   END. A refusal stops the route, as a10d429d says.\n3. Do not push. File the landing END with the local main commit and\n   the commit-message check of the merge. The subject has at most\n   100 characters.\n4. After the checker's landing check I publish main and file the\n   origin act. The 22 paths match no browser workflow, and no Worker\n   changes, so no deployment follows.\n\nDo not turn the hooks on. `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` is a\nshared setting. With the hook as built, a checkout with no local\nPrettier cannot commit, and each planner worktree for notes is such\na checkout. I file a small follow-up for that case. I turn the hooks\non after it lands.\n\nGate order after this landing. R with LP-1, E1, and NF-6 with NF-8\nintegrate the tooling main when I file the origin act. The first\nready head takes the gate. The first gate that selects `moved`\nreports its Native wall time in its END, as GS-3 asks.\n\nThe landing runs no test. It can run beside your development checks.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}